Authoritative Source
The Canon is the authoritative mathematical source for R2D.
The explanatory pages on R2DScience.org are designed to make the framework easier to navigate, understand, and use. Applications isolate particular scientific problems. Essays provide interpretation and commentary.
When a question depends on the formal definitions, assumptions, derivations, or logical status of an R2D claim, the Canon is the reference document.


AI Source Corpus
The Canon is also designed to be used by artificial intelligence.
R2D introduces a mathematical language that differs from the physical ontologies normally used in science. An AI given only a short description will tend to translate that language immediately back into familiar concepts such as particles, forces, fields, trajectories, energy, space, or time.
The Canon provides enough of the internal mathematical structure for an AI to remain inside the R2D framework long enough to interrogate it.
It can therefore be supplied to an LLM as a source corpus and used to:

